{"id":"neet-2023-q021","pn":21,"y":"NEET 2023 · 7 May","tp":"Motion in a Plane","st":"Projectile maximum height","q":"A bullet is fired from a gun at the speed of 280 ms⁻¹ in the direction 30° above the horizontal. The maximum height attained by the bullet is (g = 9.8 ms⁻², sin 30° = 0.5) :","o":["3000 m","2800 m","2000 m","1000 m"],"c":3,"s":"Maximum height H = u² sin²θ/2g.\nH = (280)² × (0.5)²/(2 × 9.8).\n= 280 × 280 × 0.5 × 0.5/19.6.\nH = 1000 m."},
{"id":"neet-2022r-q013","pn":13,"y":"Re-NEET 2022 · 4 Sep","tp":"Motion in a Plane","st":"Projectile maximum height","q":"A cricket ball is thrown by a player at a speed of 20 m/s in a direction 30° above the horizontal. The maximum height attained by the ball during its motion is.\n(g = 10 m/s²)","o":["25 m","5 m","10 m","20 m"],"c":1,"s":"Maximum height H = (u² sin²θ)/(2g).\nH = (20² × sin²30°)/(2 × 10) = (400 × 1/4)/(20) = 5 m.","sfig":{"w":150,"h":90,"alt":"Ground line with a ray rising at 30 degrees to the horizontal and the angle marked.","d":[["l",10,70,140,70],["l",30,70,102.74613391789285,28,"a"],["p","M54 70A24 24 0 0 0 50.8 58"],["t",60,66,"30°","s"]]}},
{"id":"neet-2022r-q026","pn":26,"y":"Re-NEET 2022 · 4 Sep","tp":"Motion in a Plane","st":"Scalar and vector product","q":"If F = 2î + ĵ − k̂ and r = 3î + 2ĵ − 2k̂, then the scalar and vector products of F and r have the magnitudes respectively as:","o":["10, 2","5, √3","4, √5","10, √2"],"c":3,"s":"Scalar product: F·r = 2×3 + 1×2 + (−1)(−2) = 10.\nVector product: F × r = î(−2+2) − ĵ(−4+3) + k̂(4−3) = ĵ + k̂.\nIts magnitude is √(1²+1²) = √2.\nSo the magnitudes are 10 and √2."},
{"id":"neet-2022-q048","pn":48,"y":"NEET 2022 · 17 Jul","tp":"Motion in a Plane","st":"Projectile motion at highest point","q":"A ball is projected with a velocity, 10 ms⁻¹, at an angle of 60° with the vertical direction. Its speed at the highest point of its trajectory will be","o":["5√3 ms⁻¹","5 ms⁻¹","10 ms⁻¹","Zero"],"c":0,"s":"60° with the vertical means 30° with the horizontal.\nAt the highest point the vertical velocity is zero.\nThe speed is the horizontal component = 10 cos 30° = 5√3 m/s.","sfig":{"w":300,"h":120,"alt":"Projectile path: launch velocity 10 m/s at 60 degrees to the vertical (30 degrees to the ground); at the top a horizontal arrow marks 10cos30°.","d":[["l",10,105,150,105],["l",22,98,22,22,"d"],["l",22,98,83,63,"a"],["t",76,92,"10 m/s"],["c",22,98,5],["p","M22 78A20 20 0 0 1 39.3 88"],["p","M50 98A28 28 0 0 0 46.2 84"],["t",25,58,"60°","s"],["t",54,101,"30°","s"],["p","M22 98C25 93.3 31.2 78.3 40 70C48.8 61.7 62.5 53.8 75 48C87.5 42.2 99.3 38 115 35C130.7 32 154 29.5 169 30C184 30.5 193.2 33.3 205 38C216.8 42.7 230.5 51 240 58C249.5 65 256.5 73.5 262 80C267.5 86.5 271.2 94.2 273 97"],["c",169,30,5],["l",178,24,206,24,"a"],["t",210,28,"10cos30°"]]}},
{"id":"neet-2021-q044","pn":44,"y":"NEET 2021 · 12 Sep","tp":"Motion in a Plane","st":"Projectile motion","q":"A car starts from rest and accelerates at 5 m/s². At t = 4s, a ball is dropped out of a window by a person sitting in the car. What is the velocity and acceleration of the ball at t = 6 s? (Take g = 10 m/s²)","o":["20√2 m/s, 10 m/s²","20 m/s, 5 m/s²","20 m/s, 0","20√2 m/s, 0"],"c":0,"s":"Car speed at t = 4 s: v = 5 × 4 = 20 m/s. The ball leaves with this horizontal speed and zero vertical speed.\nAfter leaving, only gravity acts (air ignored): horizontal speed stays 20 m/s, acceleration is g = 10 m/s² downward.\nAt t = 6 s the ball has fallen for 2 s: vy = 10 × 2 = 20 m/s.\nSpeed = √(20² + 20²) = 20√2 m/s.\nAcceleration = 10 m/s²."},
{"id":"neet-2021-q049","pn":49,"y":"NEET 2021 · 12 Sep","tp":"Motion in a Plane","st":"Projectile motion","q":"A particle moving in a circle of radius R with a uniform speed takes a time T to complete one revolution. If this particle were projected with the same speed at an angle 'θ' to the horizontal, the maximum height attained by it equals 4R. The angle of projection, θ, is then given by :","o":["θ = sin⁻¹((2gT²)/(π²R))^(1/2)","θ = cos⁻¹((gT²)/(π²R))^(1/2)","θ = cos⁻¹((π²R)/(gT²))^(1/2)","θ = sin⁻¹((π²R)/(gT²))^(1/2)"],"c":0,"s":"Speed on the circle: U = 2πR/T.\nMaximum height of a projectile: H = U² sin²θ/(2g) = 4R.\nsin²θ = 8gR/U² = 8gR·T²/(4π²R²) = 2gT²/(π²R).\nθ = sin⁻¹[(2gT²/(π²R))^(1/2)]."}
